# UI polish standards

Apply these on every UI change in this repo:

## Professional appearance
- Consistent spacing, alignment, and typography
- Production-ready layouts — no sloppy gaps or misaligned panels
- Center primary content where the page design calls for it

## No overlapping elements
- Audit fixed/absolute positioning and multi-column grids
- Diagrams and dense layouts need collision handling or percent-based sizing
- Test at 600px, 900px, 1100px, and 1400px widths

## Light + dark mode contrast
- Prefer CSS variables from `app.css` (`--surface`, `--text`, `--muted`, `--border`, etc.)
- Avoid hardcoded `#fff`, `#fafafa`, `#18181b` on portal chrome (outside intentional product mocks)
- Page-specific CSS must include `[data-theme="dark"]` overrides — see `static/css/workflow-discovery.css` as reference
- Product mock interiors may stay light; mock **hosts/frames** must match the portal theme

## Before shipping
- Self-review contrast in both themes
- Check for overlap and layout breakage
- Do not ask the user to re-request polish, contrast, or overlap fixes
